---
title: 'Quick Reference'
description: 'Learn the Key Concepts of AG Charts and how to quickly use common features, including Axis Configuration, Data Elements, Interactivity and Styling.'
---

This page is a Quick Reference of popular AG Charts features for developers experienced with Charts and Graphs. Learn how to use Community features, customize your charts, and get started with Enterprise features.

{% note %}
The following sections assume a level of familiarity with common Charts concepts. If you're new to Charts in general, we recommend starting with our [Introductory Tutorial](./create-a-basic-chart/) instead.
{% /note %}

## Configuring Axis

The horizontal (X) and vertical (Y) lines in cartesian charts are referred to as chart axes, and they serve to illustrate the relationships between data points on the graph.

### Axis Types

Every chart has four axis: `top`, `bottom`, `left`, `right`, which can display either [Categorical](./axes-types/#category), [Numerical](./axes-types/#number), [Time](/axes-types/#time), and [Logarithmic](/axes-types/#log) data.

Use `axes.position` to control the position of the axis, and `axes.type` to define the type:

```js
axes: [
    {
        type: 'category', // category | grouped-category | number | log | time | ordinal-time
        position: 'bottom', // top | right | bottom | left
    },
],
```

### Axis Intervals

The [Axis Interval] determines which axis labels, grid lines and ticks are shown along the axis. Intervals can be defined in steps, values, or min/max spacing.

Use `axes.interval` to control the interval of the axis:

```js
axes: [
    {
        interval: { step: 5 }, // or { values: [0, 5, 10] } | { minSpacing: 50, maxSpacing: 100 }
    }
],
```

### Axis Labels

[Axis labels] can be formatted, rotated and configured to automatically avoid collisions. Use `axes.label` to control the appearance of the axis labels:

```js
axes: [
    {
        label: {
            minSpacing: 20,
            avoidCollisions: false, // enabled by default
            autoRotate: false, // enabled by default
            formatter: function (params) {
                return params.value * 100 + '%';
            },
        },
    },
];
```

