## Enhancing Data

Charts can be enhanced with data elements, such as [legends](./legend/), [cross lines](./cross-lines/), and [stylers](./stylers/) to provide additional information to users.

### Enabling & Configuring Legend

[Legends](./legend/) are enabled by default on the chart. Use the `legend` property to configure the legend position and size:

```js
legend: {
    position: 'bottom', // 'top', 'right', 'left',
    maxWidth: 200,
    maxHeight: 300,
}
```

Individual legend items, [Labels](./legend/#labels), [Markers](./legend/#markers) and [Lines](./legend/#line) can also be customized by using the `legend.item` property:

```js
legend: {
    item: {
        maxWidth: 130,
        paddingX: 32,
        paddingY: 8,
        label: {
            fontSize: 14,
            formatter: ({value}) => value == "Coal" ? value + " *" : value
        },
        marker: {
            size: 20,
            strokeWidth: 3,
            shape: 'diamond', // 'circle', 'square', 'cross', 'plus', 'triangle'
        },
        line: {
            strokeWidth: 4,
        },
    },
}
```

### Cross Lines

[Cross Lines](./cross-lines/) are lines or shaded areas in a chart that denote additional information or thresholds.

Use the `crossLines` property in the axis options to add a Cross Line at a specific data value on an axis:

```js
axes: [
    {
        crossLines: [
            {
                type: 'line', // or 'range'
                value: 11, // or ['Jun', 'Sep']
            },
        ],
    },
],
```

### Customizing Series & Markers

[Markers](./markers/) can be customized to change their [shape, size, and style](/markers/). Use the `series.marker` property to customize markers:

```js
series: [
    // ...
    marker: {
        shape: 'square', // defaults to 'circle'
        size: 20,
        fill: 'red',
        stroke: 'maroon',
    },
]
```

[Item Stylers](./stylers/#item-stylers) allow customization of the visual appearance of Series & Markers.

Use the `itemStyler` callback function to customize the appearance of a specific Series or Marker:

```js
series: [
    {
        itemStyler: ({ datum, xKey, fill, highlighted }) => {
            return {
                fill: datum[xKey] === 'Jul' ? (highlighted ? 'lime' : 'red') : fill,
            };
        },
    },
];
```

