## Customizing Charts

Charts can be customized with [themes](./themes/), [layouts](./layout/), [backgrounds](./background/), and [overlays](./overlays/).

### Layout

The chart will [auto-size](./layout/#chart-size) by default, taking the size of the container element and auto-sizing the chart dynamically.

Use the `width` and/or `height` options if a fixed size is required:

```js
{
    width: 800,
    height: 600,
}
```

### Background

Use `background.fill` to set the [background](./background/) of the chart to any CSS Color:

```js
background: {
    fill: 'transparent', // or RGB, HEX, HSL, HWB, or named color
},
```

### Overlays

[Custom Text](./overlays/#text) or [HTML](./overlays/#custom-overlay) can be displayed over the chart to provide additional information in certain circumstances:

```js
overlays: {
    loading: {
        text: 'Some custom loading message',
    },
    noData: {
        renderer: () => '<em>Custom message for <strong>missing data</strong></em>'
    },
    noVisibleSeries: {
        text: 'Some custom noVisibleSeries message',
    },
    unsupportedBrowser: {
        text: 'Some custom unsupportedBrowser message'
    }
},
```

